<title>NEW ZEALAND: Iddison withdraws from Saigon project.</title>
<headline>Iddison withdraws from Saigon project.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iddison Group Vietnam said on Tuesday it had withdrawn from its investment in a Saigon Water Park project, receiving back the money it invested together with interest and being released from all liability.</p>
<p>Managing Director David Seton said that the size and scope of the water park had increased beyond that originally planned, requiring a greater investment by Iddison.</p>
<p>He said the directors felt that the money required to maintain its investment in the water park could be more profitably invested in other projects.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
